-- title:
--   Special-fibre components as proper κ-curves with two affine charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{P}$ of type `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p`, a local commutative ring $O$ whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, a ring homomorphism $\rho_O : \mathrm{R}\,p \to O$ from the base ring of the package, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$. Let $R$ be a resolved model package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`, with total space `R.Y`, structure morphism `R.toBase : R.Y ⟶ Spec O`, finite node set `R.node` and widths `R.width`, and let $c$ be a component index in `X0MqComponents R.width`, that is, either one of two distinguished components or a pair consisting of a node $n$ together with an element of `Fin (R.width n - 1)`. Write $I_c =$ `R.comp c` for the associated invertible ideal sheaf on `R.Y`, with closed subscheme `(R.comp c).subscheme` and closed immersion `(R.comp c).subschemeι`. The assertion is that there exists a morphism $y$ from `(R.comp c).subscheme` to $\operatorname{Spec} \kappa$ such that: (i) $y$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ equals `(R.comp c).subschemeι` followed by `R.toBase`; (ii) $y$ is proper; (iii) `(R.comp c).subscheme` admits a `TwoAffineOpenCover`, i.e. two affine opens with affine intersection whose union is everything; (iv) for every node $n$ and every $d$ in `Fin (R.width n)`, if the point `R.edgePt n d` of `R.Y` lies in the support of $I_c$, then there is a $\kappa$-point $s : \operatorname{Spec} \kappa \to$ `(R.comp c).subscheme` with $s$ followed by $y$ the identity and with `R.edgePt n d` in the image of the underlying map of $s$ followed by `(R.comp c).subschemeι`; and (v) for every section $\sigma : \operatorname{Spec} O \to$ `R.Y` of `R.toBase` whose image of the closed point of $O$ lies in the support of $I_c$, there is likewise a $\kappa$-point $s$ of `(R.comp c).subscheme`, a section of $y$, whose image under `(R.comp c).subschemeι` contains that point.
--
--   This equips each irreducible component of the special fibre of a resolved Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0p)$ with the structure of a proper curve over the residue field $\kappa = O/(p)$, covered by two affine opens with affine intersection, and exhibits both the crossing points lying on the component and the specialisations of $O$-sections of the model as $\kappa$-rational points of it. It is used in the computation of intersection numbers on the special fibre, in [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.sum_single_add_intersectionAlpha_eq_zero_of_pullback_toDR_iso`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.sum_single_add_intersectionAlpha_eq_zero_of_pullback_toDR_iso).
